#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157144 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2331a0df-036e-55aa-adf7-ce24929b4efd" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators"}] :question/id #uuid "465cc593-e81f-5040-bc49-e42b16c0b351" :question/math-academy-id "e-7720" :question/problem "Write $\\dfrac{5x^2}{5x^2-2}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{b}{5x^2-2},$ where $a \\neq 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we subtract and add $2$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{5{x}^{2}-2}=\\frac{5{x}^{2}-2+2}{5{x}^{2}-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{x}^{2}-2+2}{5{x}^{2}-2} & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}-2}{5{x}^{2}-2}+\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}-2} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{2}{5{x}^{2}-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\na + b = 1 + 2 = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157145 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157331 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48968893-6430-5e1b-ac7a-bd36991f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"}] :question/id #uuid "0efff2c3-2e5e-5ba3-815d-8419940a5090" :question/math-academy-id "e-7721" :question/problem "Write $\\dfrac{3x^2+5}{3x^2-2x}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{bx+c}{3x^2-2x},$ where $a \\neq 0.$ What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we subtract and add $2x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}+5}{3{x}^{2}-2x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+2x+5}{3{x}^{2}-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+2x+5}{3{x}^{2}-2x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x}{3{x}^{2}-2x}+\\frac{2x+5}{3{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{2x+5}{3{x}^{2}-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5,$ and we get\n\n$$\na + b + c = 1 + 2 + 5 = 8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157146 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157332 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81690612-bbae-5d54-a65c-f280d627e051" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "79c2c218-2d4c-5e14-a60e-5f5cba22df4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7722" :question/problem "Write $\\dfrac{3x^3}{x^3+4}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{b}{x^3+4},$ where $a \\neq 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $4$ in parentheses in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}+4} & =\\frac{3({x}^{3}+4-4)}{{x}^{3}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{3}+4)+3(-4)}{{x}^{3}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{3}+4)-12}{{x}^{3}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{3}+4)-12}{{x}^{3}+4} & =\\frac{3({x}^{3}+4)}{{x}^{3}+4}+\\frac{-12}{{x}^{3}+4} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{-12}{{x}^{3}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=3$ and $b=-12,$ and we get\n\n$$\na + b = 3 + (-12) = -9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2331a0df-036e-55aa-adf7-ce24929b4efd" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fe3bafd-6ad9-5915-b88d-cc104efef4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558050} {:answer/id #uuid "7699e614-4cbe-5307-b8f1-fa86c2ef10eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558097} {:answer/id #uuid "82694113-6ad6-55be-af8a-1beb32f07fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558119} {:answer/id #uuid "e2211cf9-6317-5d96-8040-6c17a8eb9968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558319} {:answer/id #uuid "f13ff96a-8947-53cb-a1dc-0d02a813cafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7699e614-4cbe-5307-b8f1-fa86c2ef10eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558097} :answer-field/id #uuid "a21f80bd-1234-5b6e-9af6-8219c8c7671b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f9ace25-75d4-5ca3-b668-b9724a364c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-114356" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{7x}{7x+2}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{7x+2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $2$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x}{7x+2}=\\frac{7x+2-2}{7x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+2-2}{7x+2} & =\\frac{7x+2}{7x+2}+\\frac{-2}{7x+2} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-2}{7x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=-2,$ and we get \n\n$$\na+b=1+(-2)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2331a0df-036e-55aa-adf7-ce24929b4efd" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01706a26-78ad-5b87-97f5-5e1d65d2013b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557871} {:answer/id #uuid "3c27ded4-366d-5a15-aca7-3f32e856713d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557991} {:answer/id #uuid "90c540ea-a7a4-514d-b263-62d9f7211812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558150} {:answer/id #uuid "bf259c16-84c7-525f-aac3-8b6d08912634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558249} {:answer/id #uuid "e987d972-9c9e-57ba-89af-0089a7bb3853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c27ded4-366d-5a15-aca7-3f32e856713d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557991} :answer-field/id #uuid "7172de9a-aa7b-5081-8f8c-f0a055aa448c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f28ef1d-28c8-56a3-9458-640f77d37f8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114357" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{x}{x+9}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{x+9},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $9$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{x+9}=\\frac{x+9-9}{x+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+9-9}{x+9} & =\\frac{x+9}{x+9}+\\frac{-9}{x+9} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-9}{x+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=-9,$ and we get \n\n$$\na+b=1+(-9)=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157331 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48968893-6430-5e1b-ac7a-bd36991f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c101dc-d9c3-56e5-9afa-d7377f0d034d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557908} {:answer/id #uuid "86c55400-24a4-55be-8cc8-42e48433c0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558129} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b4c0a8-1b78-5b5b-b328-5c29daf86013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558225} {:answer/id #uuid "d976c08b-dabc-5fdc-b8d6-2b548ff7dddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558297} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d6bfc7-1fde-54ca-bd06-1538cf414895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b4c0a8-1b78-5b5b-b328-5c29daf86013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558225} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a82e49b-c98e-58c7-8353-c48b2437d03c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1acab4f4-f111-5afa-891d-e5bad6726d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114371" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{2}+x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{{x}^{2}+x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{2}+x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{{x}^{2}+x}+\\frac{-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=10,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-1)+10=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157332 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81690612-bbae-5d54-a65c-f280d627e051" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "509f63d0-9e90-5989-8960-74a322826bb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558020} {:answer/id #uuid "6951a564-cf83-5085-a483-595121cdb640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558067} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf2e9af-604e-5bcc-83a5-288f2ddce279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558206} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b2b194-3ff7-52a1-83d3-6b70fbcdeebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558317} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4bd510-ca56-54f0-b9d1-66d799f1f856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1b2b194-3ff7-52a1-83d3-6b70fbcdeebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558317} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a1e417-0ed2-5696-a763-022509e026bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3598bce-4582-5b46-b7ba-24890d62ca14" :question/math-academy-id "q-114378" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{35{x}^{4}}{7{x}^{3}+2}$ in the form $ax+\\frac{bx}{7{x}^{3}+2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator to put $7{x}^{3}$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $2$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{35{x}^{4}}{7{x}^{3}+2} & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3})}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2-2)}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)+5x(-2)}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2} & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)}{7{x}^{3}+2}+\\frac{-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =5x+\\frac{-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=5$ and $b=-10,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=5+(-10)=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157332 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81690612-bbae-5d54-a65c-f280d627e051" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18661dc1-9e3e-5141-806d-50b4ce8fa902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557923} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1c5079-398e-55dc-aa2f-d1b31b3e4d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558078} {:answer/id #uuid "78b7d98b-486b-5166-8ccc-4aa05e0d2c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558103} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd7214b-4cc1-5256-9637-dbf607eef23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558276} {:answer/id #uuid "faffeaba-fc3e-5c99-a4ca-fb83efda4bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d1c5079-398e-55dc-aa2f-d1b31b3e4d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558078} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fdfc8ac-e680-5bff-b738-9a37de20e578" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07ef510c-76b5-598c-aa32-333fcc3beed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114380" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{9x}{x+2}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{x+2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $2$ in parentheses in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9x}{x+2} & =\\frac{9(x+2-2)}{x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9(x+2)+9(-2)}{x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9(x+2)-18}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9(x+2)-18}{x+2} & =\\frac{9(x+2)}{x+2}+\\frac{-18}{x+2} \\\\  & =9+\\frac{-18}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=9$ and $b=-18,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=9+(-18)=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157332 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81690612-bbae-5d54-a65c-f280d627e051" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801d4e3f-6db0-5039-b36e-e65b87771edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "801d4e3f-6db0-5039-b36e-e65b87771edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558116} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c08733b-1d4b-5d7f-a806-6c56e003ca4b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb087daf-4497-5358-8425-d16006c4479e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb087daf-4497-5358-8425-d16006c4479e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558360} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5891570-1568-5839-bb2a-008b6e2999e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b155ae79-db25-5713-9df8-dcb032b3bfcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-270234" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{4x-5}$ in the form $ax+\\frac{bx}{4x-5},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$8{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$x\\,+\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$4x-5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$4x-5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator to put $4x$ in parentheses. Then, we subtract and add $5$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{4x-5} & =\\frac{2x(4x)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5+5)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x[(4x-5)+(5)]}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)+2x(5)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)+10x}{4x-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x(4x-5)+10x}{4x-5} & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)}{4x-5}+\\frac{10x}{4x-5} \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{10x}{4x-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157331 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48968893-6430-5e1b-ac7a-bd36991f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4a0dda5-3965-51eb-a064-e125c2a6dbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4a0dda5-3965-51eb-a064-e125c2a6dbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558194} :answer-field/id #uuid "19a807f2-fc7c-57ce-91b1-e2110887ac9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d463ab-1161-57c6-8111-a4680bc5d096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5d463ab-1161-57c6-8111-a4680bc5d096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558288} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f59d890-8ce5-5936-9ce2-13b82c854112" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17e676f6-405b-542f-93f8-e4914767ef36" :question/math-academy-id "q-320743" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{8{x}^{5}-9}{8{x}^{5}+4}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{8{x}^{5}+4},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$8{x}^{5}-9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$8{x}^{5}+4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$8{x}^{5}+4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $4$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{5}-9}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\,=\\,\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4} & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}+4}{8{x}^{5}+4}+\\frac{-4-9}{8{x}^{5}+4} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-13}{8{x}^{5}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157331 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48968893-6430-5e1b-ac7a-bd36991f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0019261d-e016-5c70-b42a-4b7ca8e30db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557869} {:answer/id #uuid "141b0751-ebe1-57c9-a4fa-6d832b567f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557914} {:answer/id #uuid "438876c4-3834-5725-98a6-440a583de4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558001} {:answer/id #uuid "77a4321f-cfd3-5456-9203-89c805823405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558099} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ffe278-2425-59b8-bf23-a730757506c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ffe278-2425-59b8-bf23-a730757506c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558296} :answer-field/id #uuid "eba6a572-2385-5d57-b06f-21037d2d14fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5302353a-429f-5452-b2c3-3eb347800cb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-88259" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{2{x}^{2}-3},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we subtract and add $3$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3+3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3+3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3}{2{x}^{2}-3}+\\frac{3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{4}{2{x}^{2}-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=4,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=1+4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157331 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48968893-6430-5e1b-ac7a-bd36991f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ffde74b-3302-50c9-b81d-0948d05221d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557934} {:answer/id #uuid "432eac45-0632-51c2-9d7b-ee1dd3ef9d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558000} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fdf79a-af79-5d84-8b5a-5418b7dc1fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558190} {:answer/id #uuid "b8f95f45-01f0-50c7-9671-6e8a11ba2370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558237} {:answer/id #uuid "d2fdccc0-856f-51a7-a011-3e60a985cacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2fdf79a-af79-5d84-8b5a-5418b7dc1fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558190} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9cea2a-f648-53e6-920a-6b2b123f56c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31144732-cb63-5daa-92f1-95264dc5b28a" :question/math-academy-id "q-88262" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{4{x}^{3}-1}{4{x}^{3}+x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{4{x}^{3}+x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{3}-1}{4{x}^{3}+x}=\\frac{4{x}^{3}+x-x-1}{4{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{3}+x-x-1}{4{x}^{3}+x} & =\\frac{4{x}^{3}+x}{4{x}^{3}+x}+\\frac{-x-1}{4{x}^{3}+x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-x-1}{4{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-1,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$"}]}
